# Keep every text file LF in the working tree, whatever core.autocrlf is set to
# on the machine that cloned the repo. These sources are consumed inside Linux
# containers and by CI, and a CRLF checkout breaks them in ways that look like
# code faults: bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r` as an invalid option and exits
# 2, leaving the Redpanda topics uncreated, and `gofmt -l` flags every Go file
# so `task lint` fails on a clean tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
